Add-time hashing and automatic repair verification must use the resolver's git-normalized canonicalization and line-count validation. RepairContentCache captures each physical file once, normalizes that same snapshot under each required path-rule context, and supplies context and drift repair. Exact relocation normally retains the recorded hash; changing it for destination-path normalization is valid only when the same physical bytes still match the recorded identity under the original path's rules. commit.rs and the captured-byte normalizer in resolver/layers/worktree.rs must preserve that canonical byte and extent identity across EOL normalization, ident expansion, and clean/smudge filters.
